## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`Stack`): The Contentstack SDK Stack client is initialized here without live_preview config. This is the single point where the CMS connection is established — all content flows through getEntry/getSingleEntry which instantiate ContentstackFactory with this Stack. Without live_preview enabled at Stack creation, the SDK never establishes the real-time preview connection, so no downstream component (ContentstackContext, useContent, 110+ consumers) can ever receive live preview data. The symptom (no live preview) is caused here at the source, not in any presentation component.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add live_preview configuration to the `options` object before it is passed to contentstack.Stack(). The options object (defined above line 69 in the same file) needs a `live_preview` property: `live_preview: { enable: true, host: CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_HOST }` where CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_HOST is a new env variable (or hardcoded to 'https://live.contentstack.com'). This is the standard Contentstack SDK mechanism — the Stack constructor accepts live_preview in its config to enable the real-time preview websocket/polling connection. Additionally, the ContentstackContext provider (src/context/ContentstackContext.ts) will need to react to live preview data updates, but the root cause is the missing Stack-level configuration.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- Given a content editor is viewing a page on the GO Transit site in preview mode, when the editor saves a change to that page's content in the CMS, then the updated content appears on the previewed page without the editor manually reloading the page or publishing the entry.
- Given a content editor is viewing a page on the UP Express site in preview mode, when the editor saves a change to that page's content in the CMS, then the updated content appears on the previewed page without the editor manually reloading the page or publishing the entry.
- Given a content editor is viewing a page on the MX site in preview mode, when the editor saves a change to that page's content in the CMS, then the updated content appears on the previewed page without the editor manually reloading the page or publishing the entry.
- Given a content editor opens a preview session from each of the GO Transit, UP Express, and MX sites, when the editor edits brand-specific content in the CMS, then each site's preview displays that brand's own updated content and styling, with no content from another brand shown.
- Given a content editor is previewing a page that contains an expandable accordion section, when the editor saves a change to the accordion's items in the CMS, then the accordion section on the previewed page shows the updated items without a manual page reload.
- Given a content editor is previewing a page that contains a branded coloured content block, when the editor saves a change to that block's content or colour in the CMS, then the block on the previewed page shows the updated content and colour without a manual page reload.
- Given a content editor is previewing a page that contains a group of links, when the editor saves a change to those links in the CMS, then the link group on the previewed page shows the updated links without a manual page reload.
- Given a content editor is in an active preview session, when the preview session is interrupted, then the page continues to display the last available content rather than showing a broken or blank page, and the editor can resume previewing after reconnecting.
- Given a content editor is previewing a page, when the editor saves a change to the site's navigation menu entries in the CMS, then the header navigation menu shown at the top of the previewed page displays the updated entries without a manual page reload.

